Control refactoring
-------------------
Control package only: Controller.java, ControllerInterface.java,
WebServer.java, MessageManager.java, and the wiring in TopSecret.java.
Run: .\gradlew cleanTest test --console=plain

1) Re-run the suite first.
Shipped run is 305/309, 4 failures in MessageManagerSQLiteDataStoreTest
(file-lock on TempDir cleanup). WebViewWebServerTest (17 tests) has no
recorded run. Without a green baseline you cannot tell a refactor
regression from a failure that was already there.

2) Fix addEntry and editEntry on a short field list.
Controller.java:256,295. They only catch IllegalArgumentException, but
fields.get(0..4) throws IndexOutOfBoundsException on a short list. Check
fields.size() first, or catch it too. The terminal always sends a full
list. A web POST will not.

3) Log edits.
LoggedAction has only READ = 0 and CREATE = 1. Add EDIT = 2, and add one
audit.log line in editEntry (Controller.java:331). Without it every web
edit is unaudited. reviewAuditLog already prints any other value as
"edit", so nothing else changes.

4) Collapse the 8 audit blocks into one helper.
Controller.java:215,225,235,245 and 263,269,275,281. Same 3 lines, 8
times: getUserByUsername, a null check, audit.log. One helper means the
EDIT line from item 3 is a 9th call, not a 9th copy.

5) Use switch on itemType, not 4 if-else chains.
Controller.java has itemType.equals 18 times: browseMainMenu, listEntries,
readEntry, addEntry, editEntry. A switch with the same 4 cases and the
same default ("Invalid option") makes adding "countries" one case per
method. Keep itemType a String. The web passes it as a query parameter.

6) Split WebServer.start() into one handler per route.
WebServer.java:52-234. start() is 183 lines: 6 local lambdas and 6 route
handlers in one method. Extract the two pure helpers first (escape,
parseForm), then one handler per route. start() then only creates the
server and registers the routes. Do not change routing or cookies in
this change.

7) Collapse the two agent-by-name scans into one lookup.
Controller.java:373 and 396. sendMessage and viewMessages both loop
listAgents() and take the first name match, case-insensitively. One
lookup does it once. Do not cache agents in the controller. Each call
loads the whole list, which is fine at this size, and a cache would go
stale on every agent add.

8) Fix viewMessages formatting and narrow the try.
Controller.java:394-419. It has "}try{" on one line, blank lines inside,
and the try wraps the whole body. Only retrieveMessages can throw, so
only that call belongs in the try. Zero behaviour change.

9) Fix the stale comments.
Controller.java:24 says "main menu 1-9". It is 1-11. Controller.java:140
says users see "1-5 and 9". They see 1-5, 9 and 11. WebServerTest.java
says the integration file "is in recoverable trash until then". It exists.

10) Cache isAdmin once in showMainMenu.
Controller.java:142-163 calls access.isAdmin twice for the same username.
One boolean at the top, used for both admin blocks. One line, zero risk.

11) Guard the login POST body, and say what sendPage does.
WebServer.java:162 reads the whole body with no limit. Cap it, or reject
a large Content-Length with an error page. WebServer.java:117-126 catches
IOException and ignores it. Keep the behaviour, state the decision.

Do not:
- Split Controller into one controller per type. It is 420 lines, and the
split breaks ControllerTest (58 tests), TerminalView, and WebServer for
no measured benefit. Item 5 is the proportionate version.
- Rename public methods. The names are HW5/HW6 settled, and the views
and tests use them.
- Change String-returning methods to return objects. The String contract
is the terminal/web seam: the same text to the terminal, wrapped in HTML
for web.
- Add caching in the controller. See item 7.

Order: 1, then 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, then 8-11. Do 7 with the feature, since the
feature needs the same lookup. Update Docs/Control in the same commit as
the code, never separately.